ep() detects a blacklisted payout address or a      failed isBlacklisted probe. Cleared by resolveQuarantine().\"}},\"title\":\"Slot\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"balance()\":{\"notice\":\"ERC-20 USDC balance of this slot (6-decimal units).\"},\"initialize(address,bytes32,uint16,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Called exactly once by SlotFactory immediately after cloning.\"},\"resolveQuarantine(address,address,uint16)\":{\"notice\":\"Called by the current merchant to resolve a quarantine.         Allows replacing BOTH the merchant and the feeRecipient so that         a subsequent sweep can succeed regardless of which address caused         the quarantine. This is the ONLY function that may change merchant         or feeRecipient, and only from the quarantined state.         Validation mirrors initialize():         - newMerchant must be non-zero.         - If newFeeBps > 0 then newFeeRecipient must be non-zero.         - newFeeBps must be <= 1000.\"},\"sweep()\":{\"notice\":\"Permissionless sweep. Forwards USDC to merchant and feeRecipient,         reimbursing the caller for gas (in USDC) plus a flat tip.         Checks-Effects-Interactions order:           1. Checks       : balance, blacklist probes           2. Effects      : quarantine flag written if needed           3. Interactions : SafeERC20 transfers, then event         ReentrancyGuard prevents a reentrant call between transfers.\"}},\"notice\":\"A minimal deposit-address clone in the Arc Slot system.         Arc specifics honoured throughout:         - USDC is the native gas token AND an ERC-20 at ARC_USDC_ADDRESS.           We use ONLY the 6-decimal ERC-20 view; msg.value is never read.         - Transfers to address(0) revert on Arc, so all zero-address paths           are rejected at initialisation and quarantine-resolution time.         - No SELFDESTRUCT anywhere (would drain the contract's native           balance and leave a broken address).         - Nothing is payable.\",\"ve